itiation by gray into  his world of BDSM that's bondage  discipline domination submission sadism  and masochism just in case you didn't  know in some ways it's hard to believe  that Fifty Shades of Grey started life  as Twilight fan fiction but all that  stuff where gray tells Anna she should  stay away from him certainly reminds me  Edward and Bella in Twilight and the  Sana's male friend he wants much more  than friendship to the plus of Fifty  Shades brings with it an array of  cliches including the young  unsophisticated woman with no money who  falls for the rich sophisticated guy who  in this case happens to be just slightly  older than her yes poor Cinderella gets  her rich Prince but not without a good  spanking first then there's a cliche of  the woman who wants a bad boy or at  least an emotionally damaged one that  they can make good but there's also a  weird creepy horror vibe going on with  grey basically stalking Anna even  turning up in her home uninvited and  unannounced it reminded me a bit of the  terrible rom-com This Means War which  thought for some unknown reason that  it'd be romantic and funny to have two  male friends who were after the same  woman turning up randomly in her home  and tracking her every movement oh and  after how were introduced to grey the  scene where he hands Anna his business  card and the camera lingers over it  maybe half expect him to launch into a  discussion its coloring and lettering  Allah American Psycho the start of the  movie all feels like it happens rather  quickly  one minute Anna and Graham meeting for  the first time in the next minute  they're all hot as hell for each other  yes it never felt like there was any  real heat between the leads and their  meet-cute but while the development of  their desire did feel rushed the film  overall felt long I think it was the  ridiculous dialogue which did make me  laugh but just got more and more tedious  as a film went on obviously there's a  lot of nudity in Fifty